ntors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJII TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOTATO MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMA NORIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOTATO, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMA, NORIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A nonaqueous electrolytic solution type secondary battery composed at least of a negative electrode, a positive electrode and an electrolytic solution obtained by dissolving a lithium salt in a nonaqueous solvent, wherein the nonaqueous solvent contains 0.01 to 20 wt% of a vinylethylene carbonate represented by general formula (I), wherein R&lt;1&gt;, R&lt;2&gt;, R&lt;3&gt;, R&lt;4&gt;, R&lt;5&gt;, and R&lt;6&gt; are each independently hydrogen or C1-C4 alkyl. This battery is minimized in the decomposition of an electrolytic solution, exhibits high capacity, and is excellent at high temperature in preservation characteristics and cycle characteristics.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une batterie secondaire du type à solution électrolytique non aqueuse comprenant au moins une électrode négative, une électrode positive, et une solution électrolytique obtenue par dissolution d'un sel de lithium dans un solvant non aqueux, ledit solvant non aqueux renfermant de 0,01 à 20 % en poids d'un carbonate de vinyl-éthylène représenté par la formule générale (I); où R&lt;1&gt;, R&lt;2&gt;, R&lt;3&gt;, R&lt;4&gt;, R&lt;5&gt; et R&lt;6&gt; représentent chacun indépendamment hydrogène ou un alkyle en C1-C4. Cette batterie présente une décomposition minime de la solution électrolytique, une grande capacité, et elle est excellente à haute température en termes de caractéristiques de préservation et de cycle.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>